Article 3 (Scope of Submission of Cost Estimates)
(1) Where a Member of the National Assembly, a committee, or the Government introduces, proposes or submits a bill that entails costs, or where a bill amended by a committee entails costs, a cost estimate shall be attached: Provided, That this shall not apply to a bill falling under any of the following: <Amended on July 24, 2015.>
1. Where the expected cost is less than one billion won (1,000,000,000 won) on annual average, or the total cost is less than three billion won (3,000,000,000 won) in the case of temporary expenditure;
2. Where the subject of the cost estimate involves national security or military secrets;
3. Where costs are technically difficult to estimate because, for example, the bill is drafted in declaratory or recommendatory terms.
(2) Where a cost estimate is not attached pursuant to the proviso to paragraph (1), a statement of the reasons therefor shall be submitted as prescribed by regulations.
